title: Hover returns nothing for a global enum reached through a workspace namespace (B052 ancestor walk)
updated_at: "2026-08-30T23:10:54Z"
---
Found 2026-08-31 while evaluating the B056 review. Not fixed by B056; the
review's `f7d99b7` carries a candidate fix that was held back as out of scope.

## Actual Behavior

    namespace Foo {}
    void main() { Foo::VirtualKey value; }

The checker ACCEPTS `Foo::VirtualKey` - B052's ancestor walk makes a
workspace-declared namespace a real scope, and `VirtualKey` is a globally
visible enum. Hover on it returns nothing.

`hover()` (`src/server/hover.rs`) asks `lookup_external`, which consults only
`index.source_reference_key`. That is an index-only view and does not know
workspace-declared namespaces participate in the walk, so the spelling the
checker just accepted has no hover.

## Expected Behavior

Hover shows the enum, matching what the checker accepts. The two must not
disagree about whether a spelling names something.

## Scope note

This is the editor half of a resolver/surface split. The resolver half - a
global enum keyed under a synthetic module canonicalizing to its spelling
rather than its key - was a genuine B056 defect and is fixed separately by
`fix B056: a global enum canonicalizes to its KEY through any scope`. With
that in place `canonicalize_type_name` is a usable source of the canonical
key for a hover fix, which it was not before.

## Related

B052 (ancestor walk), B056 (source names), B063 (member completion omits
injected methods - same family: a surface disagreeing with the checker).